{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "למועדה", :translit "l'mo'adah", :gloss "to its appointed time"} {:he "ששה ימים בשבוע חייב בתפילין", :translit "shisha yamim ba-shavua chayav be-tefillin", :gloss "six days of the week one is obligated in tefillin"} {:he "ששה ימי מועד שאין בהם תפילין", :translit "shisha yemei mo'ed she-ein bahem tefillin", :gloss "six festival days on which there is no tefillin"} {:he "שמ\"ע", :translit "shin-mem-ayin", :gloss "acronym for the six festival days"} {:he "פארך חבוש", :translit "pe'arech chavush", :gloss "your bound turban"} {:he "אלו תפילין", :translit "eilu tefillin", :gloss "these are tefillin"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :notarikon, :word "שמ\"ע", :expansion ["פסח" "עצרת" "ראש השנה" "יום הכפורים" "סוכות"]} {:kind :gematria, :a "פארך חבוש", :b "אלו תפילין"}], :frame {:text "Tefillin are worn on weekdays but not on Shabbat or Yom Tov, since Shabbat and Yom Tov are themselves an 'ot' (sign), making tefillin unnecessary (Menachot 36a). The phrase 'pe'arech chavush' appears in Ezekiel 24:17 and 24:23. The acronym שמ\"ע compresses the six festival days exempt from tefillin: two days of Pesach, one day of Shavuot (Atzeret), one day of Rosh HaShanah, one day of Yom HaKippurim, and one day of Sukkot.", :sources ["Menachot 36a" "Ezekiel 24:17" "Ezekiel 24:23"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מימים ימימה", :translit "miyamim yamimah", :gloss "from days to days"} {:he "מימים ימימה תלכנה", :translit "miyamim yamimah telakhnah", :gloss "from days to days she would go"} {:he "חג לה' בשילה מימים ימימה", :translit "chag la-Shem be-Shiloh miyamim yamimah", :gloss "a festival to the Lord in Shiloh from days to days"} {:he "ועלה האיש ההוא מעירו מימים ימימה", :translit "ve-alah ha-ish ha-hu me-iro miyamim yamimah", :gloss "and that man would go up from his city from days to days"} {:he "והעלתה לו מימים ימימה", :translit "ve-he'elata lo miyamim yamimah", :gloss "and she would bring up to him from days to days"} {:he "מימים ולא כל ימים", :translit "miyamim ve-lo kol yamim", :gloss "from days and not all days"} {:he "למעוטי שבתות וימים טובים", :translit "l'mo'otei shabbatot ve-yamim tovim", :gloss "to exclude Sabbaths and festivals"} {:he "ימימה", :translit "yamimah", :gloss "to days"} {:he "חג ה'", :translit "chag Hashem", :gloss "festival of the Lord"} {:he "נשים נמי פטורות מן התפילין", :translit "nashim nami peturot min ha-tefillin", :gloss "women too are exempt from tefillin"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 5, :occurrences ["מימים ימימה" "מימים ימימה תלכנה" "חג לה' בשילה מימים ימימה" "ועלה האיש ההוא מעירו מימים ימימה" "והעלתה לו מימים ימימה"]}], :frame {:text "The midrashic reading 'miyamim' — 'from days' and not all days — excludes Shabbat and Yom Tov from tefillin (Eruvin 96a). Women are exempt from time-bound positive commandments including tefillin, derived in Berakhot 20a from the phrase 'u-k'shartam,' which men are commanded but women are not. Elkanah's annual pilgrimage to Shiloh is described at 1 Samuel 1:3, and Hannah's bringing of the young Samuel at 1 Samuel 2:19. Jephthah's daughter went roaming 'miyamim yamimah' at Judges 11:39. The phrase 'chag la-Shem be-Shiloh miyamim yamimah' appears at Judges 21:19.", :sources ["Eruvin 96a" "Berakhot 20a" "1 Samuel 1:3" "1 Samuel 2:19" "Judges 11:39" "Judges 21:19"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :notarikon, :word "שמ\"ע", :expansion ["פסח" "עצרת" "ראש השנה" "יום הכפורים" "סוכות"], :initials ["פ" "ע" "ר" "י" "ס"], :by :selah, :initials-match? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "פארך חבוש", :a-value 617, :b "אלו תפילין", :b-value 617, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :masorah, :count 5, :occurrences ["מימים ימימה" "מימים ימימה תלכנה" "חג לה' בשילה מימים ימימה" "ועלה האיש ההוא מעירו מימים ימימה" "והעלתה לו מימים ימימה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "מימים ימימה", :refs ["Exodus 13:10" "Judges 11:40" "Judges 21:19" "1 Samuel 1:3" "1 Samuel 2:19"], :n 5, :lens :exact} {:phrase "מימים ימימה תלכנה", :refs ["Judges 11:40"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "